From c20c1c82d9315f0479187334f8a3d6edf2ac6196 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dmayala <dmayala@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:40:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 0036] drm/a9_eink: use guarded blocking primary flips and
 profile commit phases

Replace the full client modeset takeover on every steady frame with a
primary-FB-only validated blocking atomic commit. Keep initial enable and
DPMS on the existing modeset path, and preserve all waits and safety caps.

Require exclusive primary scanout under CRTC/plane locks, the exact transport
mode, fixed connector/encoder routing, zero-offset 448x829 unrotated geometry
and either owned FB. Refuse foreign state instead of changing it under HV.
Any failed powered neutral commit removes HV after releasing DRM locks,
before another DRM attempt or joining the producer; never record it as blank.

Own consumer FIFO50 and producer OTHER/-10 policy in kernel. Reject a late
successful drive return if the hard fault already latched. Add opt-in
elapsed phase accounting in DRM/MSM; unprofiled callers remain unchanged.

The companion Android debug-off init/gate fix and host regressions live in
the project checkout. Rebuild matching DRM core, msm and a9_eink artifacts:
this patch changes the internal atomic-commit structure.

Co-Authored-By: GPT-6.1 Sol (Codex)
